'''Heretical Flare''' is a [[debuff]] from the monster skill of the same name. It deals [[physical]] [[damage over time]]. This is NOT a [[bleeding]] ailment.

It is used by the boss [[Cato, Defiler of Light]] and its map variants [[Barthol, the Corruptor]]. In the first phase of the boss (as [[Cato, Scholar of Light]] or [[Barthol, the Pure]]), he uses {{stl|Divine Flare}} instead.

It is also existed in the boss room of [[Avarius, Reassembled]] ([[The Desecrated Chambers]]) and his/its map variant [[Woad, Mockery of Man]] ({{il|Defiled Cathedral Map}}), which has a fixed pattern and does not chase the player and their minion.

The side-boss of [[Kitava]], [[Shaman of the Feast]], also use this skill.<ref>[[Monster:Metadata/Monsters/KitavaBoss/KitavaMinionBoss6]]</ref> The side-boss has multiple variant, which one variant summon a parallel Heretical Flares.

Heretical Flare is in fact coded as a minion.<ref>[[Monster:Metadata/Monsters/InvisibleFire/InvisibleKitavaCannon]]</ref> The "monster" is not targetable and does not have a nameplate. It has a skill that deals the actual damage. For [[Avarius, Reassembled]]'s case, it is known as [[Skill:InvisibleIonKitavaCannonWickerman|InvisibleIonKitavaCannonWickerman]] internally.<ref>[[Monster:Metadata/Monsters/InvisibleFire/InvisibleKitavaCannonMoveDaemon]]</ref> 

==Monsters==
The following [[monster]]s summon Heretical Flare skills:
{{#cargo_query:
|tables=monsters
|fields=CONCAT("[[", _pageName, "|", name, "]]")=Monster names, skill_ids
|where=(skill_ids HOLDS LIKE "%KitavaCannon%" OR skill_ids HOLDS LIKE "%CannonParallelKitava%" ) AND name NOT IN ("Invisible")
|limit=100
|order by=name
}}


The following "[[monster]]s" use Heretical Flare (or similar) skills:
{{#cargo_query:
|tables=monsters
|fields=CONCAT("[[", _pageName, "|", name, "]]")=Monster names, metadata_id, skill_ids
|where=skill_ids HOLDS LIKE "%InvisibleIonKitavaCannon%" 

|limit=100
|order by=name
}}

